title: Table styling
---

# Table styling

A plain Markdown table inherits the document-wide table style from the
style file — here a full grid, a shaded header row, and a light zebra
stripe on alternating body rows.

| Component  | Version | Status   |
|------------|---------|----------|
| Firmware   | 3.9.0   | Released |
| Driver     | 2.1.4   | Released |
| Bootloader | 1.0.2   | Beta     |
| Web UI     | 5.6.0   | Released |

## Per-table overrides

To style one table differently, wrap a normal pipe table in a `table` tag
and pass attributes (the sections below show the source). Anything you
don't set is inherited from the style file, so overrides stay minimal.
Supported attributes: `borders` (`grid` / `horizontal` / `none`),
`border_color`, `edge_color`, `header_background`, `stripe` (a colour or
`none`), `column_weights`, and `cell_padding`.

### Horizontal rules, striping switched off

{% table borders="horizontal" stripe="none" %}
| Setting | Value   |
|---------|---------|
| Speed   | 1.2 m/s |
| Payload | 250 kg  |
| Battery | 48 V    |
{% /table %}

### Borderless, with a custom header fill

{% table borders="none" header_background="#d8e4f0" %}
| Phase  | Owner    |
|--------|----------|
| Design | A. Smith |
| Build  | B. Jones |
| Verify | C. Lee   |
{% /table %}

### A custom stripe and border colour

{% table stripe="#fdeaea" border_color="#e3b7b7" %}
| Risk     | Severity |
|----------|----------|
| Overheat | High     |
| Stall    | Medium   |
| Drift    | Low      |
| Jitter   | Low      |
{% /table %}

### Column weights and roomier padding

A wide first column (weights `3 1 1`) with extra cell padding.

{% table column_weights="3 1 1" cell_padding="9" %}
| Description                 | Qty | Unit |
|-----------------------------|-----|------|
| Mounting bracket, stainless | 4   | pcs  |
| Hex bolt M6×20              | 16  | pcs  |
| Cable gland                 | 2   | pcs  |
{% /table %}

### Booktabs edges (dark top/bottom rules)

`edge_color` paints the outer top/bottom rules darker than the inner ones.

{% table borders="horizontal" edge_color="#202020" stripe="none" %}
| Metric     | Before | After |
|------------|--------|-------|
| Latency    | 120 ms | 80 ms |
| Throughput | 1.0k   | 1.6k  |
{% /table %}

### A header column (row headers)

`header_column=true` makes the first column row headers — bold, shaded,
and tagged for accessibility — instead of (or as well as) the top row.
Paired with a blank header row (`| | |`, which is dropped), it gives the
classic key/value metadata table.

{% table header_column=true borders="horizontal" stripe="none" %}
| | |
|---------|--------------------------|
| Date    | 2026-05-20               |
| Version | 3.9.0                    |
| Author  | Mobile Industrial Robots |
{% /table %}
